  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 334511) recorded federal contract obligations of $10.8B for FY2026 to date. The market produced 6,491 awards with an average award size of $1.7M, and obligations fell 41.3% year over year. The Department of Defense dominates buying, obligating $8.8B. Other active agencies include the Department of Transportation with $1B and the Department of Homeland Security with $819M, while smaller agency buyers include the Department of Energy with $40.2M and National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $25.8M. FY2026 to date sits below recent full-year totals: FY21 $13.2B, FY22 $13.9B, FY23 $17B, FY24 $17.1B, and FY25 $18.4B. Large vendors listed for FY2026 to date include RAYTHEON COMPANY at multiple entries totaling several large awards, LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION in multiple entries, NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION, INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC., and ELBITAMERICA, INC. This profile reflects a defense-led, high-dollar market concentrated in a few prime contractors and the Department of Defense.",
